# Harvey LAB — do not cancel in-flight sweeps

`.github/workflows/harvey-lab-firm-knowledge.yml` uses `concurrency.cancel-in-progress: true`.

## Hard rule

**Do not `git push`** (and do not otherwise start a new Harvey LAB workflow run) on a branch that already has a **queued** or **in_progress** Harvey LAB firm-knowledge / Nemotron matrix.

Before any push to a `cursor/harvey-lab-*` branch or PR that triggers that workflow:

1. Run `gh run list --branch <branch> --limit 5`.
2. If any Harvey LAB matrix job is `queued` or `in_progress`, **stop**. Report findings only. Local commit is OK; **push is forbidden** until the user explicitly says to push, or the sweep has completed/failed/been cancelled by them.

## Not exceptions

- Partial CPR misses (e.g. task 001 at 6/7)
- Infra fixes discovered mid-run
- Cloud-agent “commit and push every iteration” defaults

Those wait. Pushing mid-sweep burns OpenRouter quota and wall clock and has already angered the operator more than once.
